nical specification (all ten protocols)"}]}],"id":"blk-73572","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-73575","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104933","marks":["bold"],"text":"spec/OS-008-HARNESS"},{"id":"spn-104934","text":" — the Agent Harness Protocol specification"}]}],"id":"blk-73574","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-73577","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104935","marks":["bold"],"text":"spec/OS-009-PRISM-SPECIFICATION"},{"id":"spn-104936","text":" — PRISM diagnostic benchmark protocol"}]}],"id":"blk-73576","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-73579","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104937","marks":["bold"],"text":"spec/OS-010-PULSE-SPECIFICATION"},{"id":"spn-104938","text":" — PULSE loop manifest standard"}]}],"id":"blk-73578","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-73581","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104939","marks":["bold"],"text":"spec/OS-E001-EMPIRICAL-EVALUATION"},{"id":"spn-104940","text":" — empirical evaluation of topology-aware continual learning"}]}],"id":"blk-73580","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-73582","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-104941","text":"Documentation index"}]},{"id":"blk-73583","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104942","text":"Linked index of every page in this set (renders on GitHub and in the docs atlas; the toctrees above drive the Sphinx build):"}]},{"id":"blk-73584","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104943","marks":["bold"],"text":"Guides"}]},{"id":"blk-73585","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-73587","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104944","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/quickstart.md"}],"text":"Quickstart"}]}],"id":"blk-73586","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-73589","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104945","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/runtime-walkthrough.md"}],"text":"Runtime Walkthrough"}]}],"id":"blk-73588","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-73591","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104946","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/positioning.md"}],"text":"Positioning — The Missing Constraint: Runtime Governance in the Agent Stack"}]}],"id":"blk-73590","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-73593","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104947","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/competitive-landscape.md"}],"text":"Competitive Landscape — Agent Governance and Runtime Enforcement"}]}],"id":"blk-73592","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-73595","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104948","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/comparison-table.md"}],"text":"Comparison — OpenSentience vs. Alternatives"}]}],"id":"blk-73594","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-73597","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104949","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/ecosystem-overview.md"}],"text":"Ecosystem Overview — How the Protocols Connect"}]}],"id":"blk-73596","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-73599","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104950","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/research.md"}],"text":"Research Overview"}]}],"id":"blk-73598","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-73601","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104951","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/faq.md"}],"text":"FAQ"}]}],"id":"blk-73600","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-73603","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104952","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/skills/SKILLS.md"}],"text":"Agent Skills"}]}],"id":"blk-73602","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-73604","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104953","marks":["bold"],"text":"Specifications"}]},{"id":"blk-73605","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-73607","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104954","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/spec/OS-011-EMBODIMENT.md"}],"text":"OS-011 — Embodiment Protocol"}]}],"id":"blk-73606","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-73609","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104955","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/spec/OS-E001-EMPIRICAL-EVALUATION.md"}],"text":"OS-E001 — Empirical Evaluation of Topology-Aware Continual Learning"}]}],"id":"blk-73608","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-73610","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104956","marks":["bold"],"text":"UX & build prompts"}]},{"id":"blk-73611","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-73613","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104957","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/ux/user-stories-embodiment.md"}],"text":"Embodiment (body-browser + body-os) — User Stories"}]}],"id":"blk-73612","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-73615","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104958","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/prompts/OS-008-BUILD.md"}],"text":"OS-008 Agent Harness Protocol — Implementation Build Prompt"}]}],"id":"blk-73614","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-73616","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-104959","text":"The Three Enforcement Layers"}]},{"id":"blk-73617","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104960","text":"OpenSentience provides three layers of runtime enforcement:"}]},{"id":"blk-73618","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"OS-008 Harness:   \"Has this agent followed the correct process?\"\n                   Pipeline ordering, quality gates, sprint contracts\n\nOS-006 Shim:      \"Is this agent allowed to do this?\"\n                   Permissions, lifecycle, autonomy levels\n\nOS-007 Security:  \"Is this agent under attack?\"\n                   Threat detection, identity verification, circuit breakers"},{"id":"blk-73619","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104961","text":"All three log to the same append-only audit trail, creating a unified compliance record from protocol to permission to pipeline."}]},{"id":"blk-73620","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-104962","text":"The Three-Protocol Stack"}]},{"id":"blk-73621","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104963","text":"Above the cognitive primitives, OpenSentience publishes three sibling protocols that together turn the [&] portfolio into a measurable, composable, accountable agent substrate:"}]},{"id":"blk-73622","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  PRISM (OS-009) — measures loops over time   diagnostic │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  PULSE (OS-010) — declares loops + signals    temporal  │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  [&] Protocol     — composes capabilities     structural│\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘"},{"head":[{"id":"blk-73624","spans":[{"id":"spn-104964","text":"Layer"}]},{"id":"blk-73625","spans":[{"id":"spn-104965","text":"Question"}]},{"id":"blk-73626","spans":[{"id":"spn-104966","text":"Artifact"}]}],"id":"blk-73623","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-73627","spans":[{"id":"spn-104967","text":"[&]"}]},{"id":"blk-73628","spans":[{"id":"spn-104968","text":"What can each agent do, and how do they compose?"}]},{"id":"blk-73629","spans":[{"id":"spn-104969","marks":["code"],"text":"*.ampersand.json"}]}],[{"id":"blk-73630","spans":[{"id":"spn-104970","text":"PULSE"}]},{"id":"blk-73631","spans":[{"id":"spn-104971","text":"How do their processes cycle and signal each other?"}]},{"id":"blk-73632","spans":[{"id":"spn-104972","marks":["code"],"text":"*.pulse.json"},{"id":"spn-104973","text":" (loop manifest)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-73633","spans":[{"id":"spn-104974","text":"PRISM"}]},{"id":"blk-73634","spans":[{"id":"spn-104975","text":"How well do those cycles actually work over time?"}]},{"id":"blk-73635","spans":[{"id":"spn-104976","text":"Diagnostic reports + leaderboards"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-73636","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104977","text":"A loop is "},{"id":"spn-104978","marks":["bold"],"text":"PULSE-conforming"},{"id":"spn-104979","text":" if its manifest validates against "},{"id":"spn-104980","marks":["code"],"text":"pulse-loop-manifest.v0.1.json"},{"id":"spn-104981","text":" and its runtime passes the 12-test conformance suite. A system is "},{"id":"spn-104982","marks":["bold"],"text":"PRISM-evaluable"},{"id":"spn-104983","text":" automatically once it is PULSE-conforming — PRISM's "},{"id":"spn-104984","marks":["code"],"text":"compose"},{"id":"spn-104985","text":" phase reads the manifest, injects scenarios at the declared "},{"id":"spn-104986","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve"},{"id":"spn-104987","text":" boundary, and observes outcomes via the declared "},{"id":"spn-104988","marks":["code"],"text":"learn"},{"id":"spn-104989","text":" phase. Adoption order is typically [&] → PULSE → PRISM."}]},{"id":"blk-73637","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-104990","text":"Relationship to the [&] Ecosystem"}]},{"id":"blk-73638","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104991","text":"OpenSentience occupies the "},{"id":"spn-104992","marks":["bold"],"text":"governance and research layer"},{"id":"spn-104993","text":" of the [&] stack:"}]},{"id":"blk-73639","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"  [&] Protocol        — capability composition (what an agent CAN do)\n  OpenSentience       — governance + harness (what an agent MAY do, and how)\n  Graphonomous        — memory + learning (OS-001, OS-002, OS-004, OS-005)\n  AgenTroMatic        — deliberation (OS-003)\n  Delegatic           — policy authoring (feeds into OS-006 enforcement)\n  Agentelic           — agent manifests (consumed by OS-006 install)\n  FleetPrompt         — marketplace (agents enter governance on install)\n  SpecPrompt          — acceptance criteria (consumed by OS-008 quality gates)"},{"id":"blk-73640","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104994","text":"The governance shim wraps any OTP "},{"id":"spn-104995","marks":["code"],"text":"child_spec"},{"id":"spn-104996","text":". It does not replace the supervised process — it interposes permission checks, lifecycle management, autonomy control, pipeline enforcement, and audit logging around it."}]},{"id":"blk-73641","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-104997","text":"Founding Thesis"}]},{"id":"blk-73642","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104998","text":"OpenSentience exists because intelligence without governance is generation without accumulation. The ten protocols formalize what structured accumulation requires: memory that consolidates, routing that detects cycles, deliberation that resolves conflict, attention that prioritizes, resources that adapt, governance that enforces boundaries, security that detects threats, a harness that orchestrates the entire pipeline, "},{"id":"spn-104999","marks":["bold"],"text":"diagnostics that measure whether the loop actually learns"},{"id":"spn-105000","text":" (PRISM), and a "},{"id":"spn-105001","marks":["bold"],"text":"temporal manifest"},{"id":"spn-105002","text":" that lets every loop in the ecosystem declare how it cycles and signals (PULSE)."}]},{"id":"blk-73643","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105003","text":"The shim is deliberately thin. Governance should cost less than 1% of the system it governs. PULSE is a manifest standard with no required runtime. PRISM runs as a separate benchmark engine that any system can opt into via its PULSE manifest."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaieraiqq4md6m4ixf5ncqwxt2zpbqfewmydhu6ky457jvz4mzvi6okqha","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}